# Content fixtures diff as PROSE, not as escaped JSON.
#
# A chapter's body_html is one JSON line — 12 KB in a small book, 190 KB in the
# largest — so `git diff` prints tens of kilobytes for a one-word fix and the
# change is invisible inside it. That matters more here than tidiness: this
# pipeline's promise is that a human reviews an AI translation before it ships,
# and an unreadable diff is how that promise quietly stops being kept.
#
# The attribute alone is INERT. Git will not let a repository install a
# textconv command (it would be arbitrary code execution on clone), so each
# clone opts in once:
#
#     cd backend && uv run python manage.py content_diff --install
#
# `manage.py content_diff` renders the same prose with no git config at all,
# which is what CI and PR review use.
backend/library/fixtures/content/**/*.json diff=ochorus-content
